cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "L8 myoblast bioprinting finite element and Gaussian process framework"
abstract: >-
  Axisymmetric finite element model (DOLFINx 0.10) of shear-thinning flow, with inertia,
  through the cartridge and nozzle of an extrusion bioprinter, coupled to the damage law of
  Ning et al. (2018) for L8 myoblasts, and a Gaussian process surrogate that maps applied
  pressure and nozzle diameter to flow rate, wall shear stress and predicted cell damage.
  Includes the 32-case simulation grid, the surrogate validation, the comparisons with
  published data and the scripts behind every figure of the accompanying article.
